---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description={`What ${SITE.name} collects, the cookies advertising and analytics set, and how to exercise your rights under the GDPR and the CCPA.`}
  lede="What is collected, who else sees it, and how to opt out."
  updated="October 25, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This page describes how {SITE.name} handles information when you visit
    <strong>{SITE.url}</strong>. There are no accounts, no newsletter and no web
    form on this site, so nothing is collected by signing up. For any privacy
    question or request, use the address on our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Information involved in a visit</h2>
  <p>
    Serving a page requires a request to the hosting provider, which records
    ordinary technical information: the IP address making the request, the page
    requested, the time, the referring page and basic browser and device
    details. These records exist to deliver the site, keep it available and
    investigate abuse.
  </p>
  <p>
    Article images are served from this site's own domain. Fonts and other
    embedded resources may be requested from their providers directly.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising and the cookies it sets</h2>
  <p>
    This site is a Google AdSense publisher, and the AdSense script is loaded on
    every page. That means third parties, not only this site, process some
    information about your visit.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Google and its advertising partners use cookies and similar identifiers to
      serve ads, limit how often you see the same ad, and measure whether ads
      work.
    </li>
    <li>
      Google's advertising cookie lets it and its partners serve ads based on
      your visits to this site and others.
    </li>
    <li>
      Third-party vendors may set their own cookies when their ads are shown.
      This publication does not control those cookies and cannot read them.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can turn off personalised advertising in
    <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer">Google's Ads Settings</a>,
    review
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>,
    and opt out of personalisation by many other vendors at
    <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer">optout.aboutads.info</a>
    or <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer">youronlinechoices.eu</a>.
    Turning off personalisation does not remove advertising; it makes the ads you
    see less specific to you.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This site uses Google Analytics to measure visits. Google may process
    information such as your IP address and online identifiers, and analytics
    may use cookies to understand how visitors move through the site. The
    reporting is aggregated rather than a record of an individual reader.
  </p>

  <h2>Consent settings</h2>
  <p>
    Google Consent Mode defaults on this site are set to denied for advertising
    storage, advertising personalisation, advertising user data and analytics
    storage. Those defaults are applied before any Google script runs.
  </p>
  <p>
    A certified consent management platform has not yet been installed here, so
    no consent banner is shown and no consent choice is recorded. The denied
    defaults above are a protective setting, not a consent mechanism, and they
    are not a substitute for the regional controls that a consent platform
    provides. This paragraph will change when one is in place.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Articles may link to retailers and other websites, including affiliate
    links. Their privacy practices apply once you visit them, and this policy
    does not cover them. See our <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a> for how
    affiliate links and advertising are handled here.
  </p>

  <h2>If you are in the UK or the European Economic Area</h2>
  <p>
    Under the UK GDPR and the EU GDPR you have the right to ask for a copy of
    the personal data held about you, to have it corrected or erased, to
    restrict or object to how it is used, to receive it in a portable form, and
    to withdraw consent you have given. You also have the right to complain to
    your national data protection authority.
  </p>
  <p>
    The lawful basis for the technical records described above is legitimate
    interest in delivering and protecting the site. The lawful basis for
    personalised advertising is consent, which you can change at any time
    through the links in the advertising section.
  </p>
  <p>
    Requests about data held by Google or another advertising vendor have to be
    made to that company, because this publication cannot access or delete
    records inside their systems.
  </p>

  <h2>If you are in California</h2>
  <p>
    Under the CCPA, as amended by the CPRA, you have the right to know what
    categories of personal information are collected and who they are disclosed
    to, to request deletion, to correct inaccurate information, and to opt out
    of the sale or sharing of personal information — which includes sharing for
    cross-context behavioural advertising. You also have the right not to be
    treated differently for exercising any of these rights.
  </p>
  <p>
    This publication does not sell personal information for money. Allowing
    advertising vendors to set identifiers may still count as sharing under the
    CCPA, so you can opt out using the advertising links above, or by writing to
    the address on our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> with "California
    privacy request" in the subject line.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site publishes home decorating guides for adults. It is not directed at
    children under 13 and no information is knowingly collected from them. If
    you believe a child has provided personal information, write to us and it
    will be deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    The date above changes whenever this policy does. Where a change materially
    affects how information is handled, the change will be described rather than
    quietly substituted.
  </p>

</PageLayout>
